2) run DECONTAM (first i need to rerun DADA2) 
to run decontam i need a column of my samples versus control. I used claude code to help me make this new column 

This makes Sample_or_Control column 
python -c "
import pandas as pd
df = pd.read_csv('metadata_with_added_cols90k.tsv', sep='\t')
sample_id_col = df.columns[0]
df['Sample_or_Control'] = 'sample'
blanks = ['blank-1_S59', 'blank-2_S60', 'blank-3_S61']
df.loc[df[sample_id_col].isin(blanks), 'Sample_or_Control'] = 'control'
df.to_csv('metadata_with_added_cols90k.tsv', sep='\t', index=False)
print(df[[sample_id_col, 'Sample_or_Control']])
"
This makes Concentration column from Quality check done by UMGC 
opened metadata .tsv file in Numbers on mac 
then manually added the concentration column and saved it back as .tsv 
we are now ready for decontam 

--- DECONTAM ---
###run decontam on feature table 
###first identify contamination 

qiime quality-control decontam-identify \
  --i-table asv-table90k.qza \
  --m-metadata-file metadata_with_added_cols90k.tsv \
  --p-method combined \
  --p-freq-concentration-column Concentration \
  --p-prev-control-column Sample_or_Control \
  --p-prev-control-indicator control \
  --o-decontam-scores comb-decontam-scores90k.qza

qiime quality-control decontam-score-viz \
